AArch64 Spinlock2
(* Test-and-set spinlock, Linux arm64 `arch_spin_lock` shape (Promising-ARM
   PLDI'19 §7 "SLA"): LDAXR/STXR acquire loop, STLR release.
   Two threads each take the lock once and increment a shared counter.
   Property: no lost update, counter = 2 in every final state.
   Expected: Always (mutual exclusion holds).
   Open: no safety theorem. Its LL/SC acquire (`LDAXR`/`STXR`) is deferred
   in the Stage 2/3 logic (Promising/EnvWP.md, "LL/SC"), so there is no
   runner-exact theorem either
   (LockFree/AArch64/README.md, "Typed headers and runner-exact theorems").
   Proved by evaluation (the explorer's verdict at fuel 300):
   `Kraken.Examples.LockFree.spinlock2_aarch64`
   (Examples/LockFree/TheoremsAArch64.lean).
   The shared symbols are typed (`uint32_t lock`, `uint32_t counter`, the width of every access)
   so that the runner declares them as sized locations at the width of
   the code's accesses (A64DECLS): the runner's
   declarations then agree with the proofs' locations. The code block and
   the verdict are unchanged. *)
# flags: -sym
# expect: Always
{
uint32_t lock=0; uint32_t counter=0;
0:X0=lock; 0:X1=counter;
1:X0=lock; 1:X1=counter;
}
threads { P0: worker done; P1: worker done; }
code {
worker:
  LDAXR W2,[X0]
  CBNZ W2,worker
  MOV W3,#1
  STXR W4,W3,[X0]
  CBNZ W4,worker
  LDR W5,[X1]
  ADD W5,W5,#1
  STR W5,[X1]
  STLR WZR,[X0]
  B done
done:
}
forall [counter]=2
